# Unused Code Prevention for AgileSpace

## Rule: Eliminate All Unused Code

This rule enforces strict removal of unused code to maintain a clean, performant, and maintainable codebase.

### ❌ Prohibited: Unused Imports

```tsx
// ❌ Bad - Unused imports
import React from "react"; // Not using React
import { Button, Card } from "@/components/ui"; // Only using Button
import type { User, Session, Tag } from "@/types"; // Only using User

export function MyComponent({ user }: { user: User }) {
  return <Button>{user.name}</Button>;
}
```

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Only necessary imports
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button";
import type { User } from "@/types";

export function MyComponent({ user }: { user: User }) {
  return <Button>{user.name}</Button>;
}
```

### ❌ Prohibited: Unused Variables

```tsx
// ❌ Bad - Unused variables
export function SessionCard({ session }: SessionCardProps) {
  const [isLoading, setIsLoading] = useState(false); // Never used
  const duration = calculateDuration(session.start_time); // Never used

  return <div>{session.title}</div>;
}
```

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Only necessary variables
export function SessionCard({ session }: SessionCardProps) {
  return <div>{session.title}</div>;
}
```

### ❌ Prohibited: Unused Functions

```tsx
// ❌ Bad - Unused helper functions
function formatDuration(ms: number): string {
  // Never called anywhere
  return `${ms / 1000}s`;
}

export function LoginForm() {
  return <form>...</form>;
}
```

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Only necessary functions
export function LoginForm() {
  return <form>...</form>;
}
```

### ❌ Prohibited: Unused Hook Returns

```tsx
// ❌ Bad - Unused hook returns
export function MyComponent() {
  const { data, loading, error, refetch } = useQuery(...) // Only using data

  return (
    <div>
      {data?.map(item => <div key={item.id}>{item.name}</div>)}
    </div>
  )
}
```

```tsx
// ✅ Good - Only destructure what's needed
export function MyComponent() {
  const { data } = useQuery(...)

  return (
    <div>
      {data?.map(item => <div key={item.id}>{item.name}</div>)}
    </div>
  )
}
```

## Detection Strategies

### 1. TypeScript Compiler Flags

- Use `"noUnusedLocals": true` in tsconfig.json
- Use `"noUnusedParameters": true` in tsconfig.json
- Regular `pnpm tsc --noEmit` checks

### 2. ESLint Rules

- `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars`
- `import/no-unused-modules`

### 3. IDE Integration

- Use VS Code's "Remove Unused Imports" command
- Enable "Organize Imports on Save"
- Use "Go to References" to verify usage

## Cleanup Commands

```bash
# Check for unused code
pnpm tsc --noEmit
pnpm eslint src/ --fix
```

## Benefits

1. **Smaller Bundle Size**: Fewer imports = smaller build output
2. **Better Performance**: Less code to parse and execute
3. **Cleaner Codebase**: Easier to read and maintain
4. **Better Tree Shaking**: Build tools can optimize better

## Enforcement

- **Pre-commit Hooks**: Run unused code checks
- **CI/CD Pipeline**: Fail builds with unused code
- **Code Reviews**: Manually check for unused imports/variables

Remember: **Every line of code has a cost**. If it's not providing value, remove it! 🧹
